<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Algonquin people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Algonquins</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Algonquin are an Indigenous people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottawa">Ottawa</a> River valley in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, whose name was later given to the wider Algonquian language family. Hunters and fur traders, they allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain">Samuel de Champlain</a> and the Huron against the Mohawk in 1609, beginning a long alliance with the French. Wars with the Iroquois in the seventeenth century drove many from their lands, and today they live in several communities in Quebec and Ontario.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/algonquin-people.jpg" alt="Algonquin people" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DarrenBaker · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anishinaabe-Anishinini_Distribution_Map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
